ings, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the production of ammonia in North America, Europe, and internationally. It operates through Ammonia, Granular Urea, UAN, AN, and Other segments. The company offers ammonia products; nitrogen products, such as granular urea, urea ammonium nitrate solution, and ammonium nitrate; diesel exhaust fluid, urea liquor, and nitric acid products. It serves cooperatives, retailers, independent fertilizer distributors, traders, wholesalers, and industrial users. The company was founded in 1946 and is headquartered in Northbrook, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher D. Bohn | CEO, President & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $2.4M ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $621K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $16K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["CF Industries Holdings, Inc. is a large-cap basic materials business with a $18.3B market cap on $7.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -14% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 37%.","The business throws off $1.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 25 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.89\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 15\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 9.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $22.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-22736647.47},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Basic Materials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 23% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 35% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 32% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","20 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Basic Materials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Financial quality scores above most Basic Materials peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Investors Are Reacting To CF Industries Holdings (CF) Strong Earnings Outlook","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-cf/cf-industries-holdings/news/how-investors-are-reacting-to-cf-industries-holdings-cf-stro","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794569465.828,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Tradeify devient le partenaire commercial officiel de l'Inter Miami CF","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/tradeify-devient-le-partenaire-commercial-officiel-de-linter-miami-cf-302936756.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794492900.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Tradeify Joins Inter Miami CF as the Club's Official Trading Partner","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/tradeify-joins-inter-miami-cf-as-the-clubs-official-trading-partner-302936752.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794492900.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Tradeify wird offizieller Handelspartner von Inter Miami CF","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/tradeify-wird-offizieller-handelspartner-von-inter-miami-cf-302936769.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794492900.0,"origin":"