ore":0.0,"weight":0.1},"market":{"score":0.0,"weight":0.1}},"data_summaries":{"sect":["Its 32% operating margin runs 23pp above the Basic Materials median (9%), a real cost or pricing edge over peers.","It captures 2.49x its revenue share in sector profits, taking a disproportionate slice of the profit pool.","It accounts for 0.4% of sector revenue and 1.1% of sector operating profit.","Over five years it has been gaining share of the sector profit pool (+18.1% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.03 across 221 companies in the universe; the top four hold 25% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 42% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 12% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 44% and a beta of 0.43, it is more defensive than the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -1.44 vs 5y 0.16), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $279.6M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 54% in the 2020 crash, 28% in the 2022 bear market and 77% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 35% below its DCF fair value of $192, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 41%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $152 to $246 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Basic Materials peers: P/E 8.8 vs 16.3, EV/EBITDA 5.6 vs 8.3 and P/FCF 10.2 vs 22.4 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 61% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are attractive: an FCF yield of 9.8% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 10.3% (vs the 8% bar).","The 20 covering analysts target $130 on average, 4% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 22% clears the cost of capital of 8.0% by 14pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.57).","It runs a 37% gross margin